.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/

# The cache holds two very different kinds of file.
#
# RAW SOURCE DATA (play-by-play, participation, weekly stats, snap counts) is
# ~100MB, is rebuildable from nflverse in minutes, and is needed only to REBUILD
# the training table. It must never be committed.
#
# DERIVED RUNTIME ARTIFACTS are small and the deployed app cannot start without
# them, because a fresh host has no way to rebuild a 63k-row backfill inside a
# web request. Those are un-ignored below.
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep
!cache/player_week_2016_2025_v1.parquet
!cache/team_week_2016_2025_v1.parquet
!cache/league_season_2016_2025_v1.parquet
!cache/availability_2025_2025_v2.parquet
!cache/availability_adj_2025_2025_v2.parquet

# The two calibration layers. WITHOUT THESE THE DEPLOYED BOARD SILENTLY REVERTS
# to gap-based leans, which is the bug the probability layer exists to fix:
# `uncertainty.available()` returns False, `prob_over` returns NaN for every row,
# and `compare()` falls back to model-minus-line. Nothing errors. A fresh clone
# was checked and did exactly that before these were un-ignored.
!cache/prob_calibration_v1.parquet
!cache/mean_calibration_v1.parquet

# Per-game weather from Open-Meteo. Committed because refetching it is 364 API
# calls against a free service, and because the backfill build reads it.
!cache/weather_2016_2026_v1.parquet

# The CURRENT season, rebuilt and committed weekly by .github/workflows/weekly.yml.
# Without it the deployed site projects mid-season as if the season had not
# started, because the ten-year backfill above is frozen and ends in 2025.
# Wildcarded by year so next season needs no edit here.
!cache/player_week_20[2-9][0-9]_20[2-9][0-9]_v1.parquet
!cache/team_week_20[2-9][0-9]_20[2-9][0-9]_v1.parquet

# Pasted boards and their FROZEN projections are COMMITTED, because the
# published site has no persistent disk and the accuracy record must not be
# per-deployment state. Anything written at runtime there dies on the next
# restart, which would leave the live record silently different from this one.
#
# So the record is a build artifact: paste locally, freeze locally, commit, push.
# The deployment sets GRIDIRONVALUE_READONLY=1 and refuses to write either file,
# which also means a visitor cannot overwrite the record from the public site.
#
# Cost is roughly 800KB per week of the season. Worth it: without these two the
# published site has no board and no record.
!cache/pp_lines_*.json
!cache/pp_frozen_*.json

# Per-week projections are derived from the committed artifacts and are
# regenerated on demand, version-stamped in the filename.
cache/predictions_*.parquet
